# Day 10 – UART Shell

## Objective

Implemented a UART command-line shell for monitoring and controlling the EV ADAS system.

The UART shell allows the user to communicate with the STM32 system through a serial terminal.

## Features

- UART command reception
- Ring buffer for received data
- Command parsing
- Character echo
- EV drive mode selection
- Speed injection
- SOC injection
- Motor temperature injection
- Obstacle distance injection
- Fault injection
- Fault clearing
- Alarm testing
- Complete system status display
- System reset command
- Help command

## Supported Commands

```text
mode <eco|normal|sport>
speed set <kmh>
soc set <pct>
temp set <degC>
obstacle <cm>
obstacle clear
fault inject <motor|soc|col>
fault clear
alarm test
status
reset
help
